="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mons-graupius">Mons Graupius</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">c. 122</span><span class="rf-text">Building begins on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hadrians-wall">Hadrian's Wall</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-tyne">Tyne</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solway-firth">Solway</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">286</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carausius">Carausius</a> declares himself emperor and rules <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> independently until 293</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">306</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-i">Constantine the Great</a> is proclaimed emperor at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york">York</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">367</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/picts">Picts</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scoti">Scotti</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxons</a> overrun the province in the 'barbarian conspiracy'</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">410</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honorius">Honorius</a> reportedly tells the cities of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> to look to their own defence</span></li></ol>
